  "notes": "Godan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), く row.\n- Negative: {欺|あざむ}かない\n- Polite: {欺|あざむ}きます\n- Te-form: {欺|あざむ}いて\n- Past: {欺|あざむ}いた\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive ({他動詞|たどうし}).\n\nUSAGE:\nA literary and somewhat formal word. In everyday conversation, だます or {騙|だま}す is more common. {欺|あざむ}く appears frequently in novels, news, and formal speech. It often implies a moral judgment against the deceiver.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {人|ひと}を{欺|あざむ}く: to deceive people\n- {世間|せけん}を{欺|あざむ}く: to deceive the world/public\n- {目|め}を{欺|あざむ}く: to fool the eye, to deceive\n- {自分|じぶん}を{欺|あざむ}く: to deceive oneself\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- だます: to trick, to deceive (everyday, casual)\n- {偽|いつわ}る: to falsify, to misrepresent (formal/literary)\n- {誤魔化|ごまか}す: to fudge, to cover up (colloquial)",
